BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:british-council-connections-through-culture-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:Deadline: Connections Through Culture Grants 2026 (British Council)
DESCRIPTION:Connections Through Culture (CTC) grants are designed to enable
  meaningful partnerships\, cross-cultural exchange and long-term collabora
 tion between the UK and participating countries. In 2026\, CTC incorporate
 s the grants programmes formerly known as Biennials Connect (Visual Arts) 
 and Architecture\, Design and Fashion Biennials and Festivals Grants\, and
  serves as the British Council's major Arts grants programme for 2026 (in 
 place of International Collaboration Grants). It offers grants of between 
 GBP 5\,000 and GBP 15\,000 to support creative practitioners\, cultural pr
 ofessionals\, artists\, organisations\, festivals\, biennials\, hubs and c
 ollectives to develop and deliver collaborative projects across a wide ran
 ge of themes and art forms\, including applied arts\, architecture\, curat
 ing\, dance\, design\, digital\, drawing\, education\, fashion\, film\, in
 stallation\, interdisciplinary work\, painting\, performance\, photography
 \, printmaking\, public art\, research\, sculpture\, social practice\, sou
 nd art\, textiles\, video\, visual arts and writing. ELIGIBILITY: applicat
 ions must involve collaboration between at least one UK-based partner and 
 at least one partner based in an eligible participating country\; each par
 tner must be legally based in the country they are applying from at the ti
 me of application and throughout the project activity period. PARTICIPATIN
 G COUNTRIES: Albania\, Argentina\, Australia\, Bangladesh\, Bosnia and Her
 zegovina\, Colombia\, Mainland China\, Egypt\, Indonesia\, Kazakhstan\, Ke
 nya\, Kosovo\, Lebanon\, Malaysia\, Mexico\, Montenegro\, New Zealand\, Ni
 geria\, North Macedonia\, Pakistan\, Palestine\, Peru\, Philippines\, Saud
 i Arabia\, Serbia\, South Africa\, Tanzania\, Thailand\, Tunisia\, Turkey\
 , United Arab Emirates\, UK\, Ukraine\, Uzbekistan\, Venezuela\, and Vietn
 am. Eligible applicants include artists and creative practitioners\, arts 
 and cultural organisations\, festivals and biennials\, cultural profession
 als\, creative hubs/networks/collectives\, and organisations working acros
 s arts\, culture and the creative sectors. Note: applications involving pr
 ojects organised by or taking place as part of Visual Arts\, Architecture\
 , Design\, Fashion and Craft festivals should be made by the festival or b
 iennial organisation rather than by individual artists\, designers or prac
 titioners. No application fee. Deadline 12 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: B
 ritish Council\nLocation: International collaboration grant. Each applicat
 ion must involve at least one UK-based partner and at least one partner ba
 sed in an eligible participating country\; each partner must be legally ba
 sed in the country they apply from throughout the project.\nAward: Grants 
 of between GBP 5\,000 and GBP 15\,000. Free to apply.\nDuration: Project-b
 ased\; develop and deliver collaborative projects across a range of themes
  and art forms.\n\nMore: https://arts.britishcouncil.org/connections-throu
 gh-culture?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arts.britishcouncil.org/connections-through-culture?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International collaboration grant. Each application must involve a
 t least one UK-based partner and at least one partner based in an eligible
  participating country\; each partner must be legally based in the country
  they apply from throughout the project.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:social-shifters-global-innovation-challenge-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Social Shifters Global Innovation Challenge 2026
DESCRIPTION:Social Shifters\, a Scottish-registered charity backed by corpo
 rate partners\, runs its Global Innovation Challenge as a funnel into a lo
 nger founder-development pipeline rather than a one-off prize. ELIGIBILITY
 : founders aged 18 to 30 at submission\, leading a fully youth-led venture
  that is already live and producing measurable social or environmental imp
 act\, aligned to at least one Sustainable Development Goal\; concept-stage
  ideas and student projects do not qualify. Multiple winners receive up to
  USD 15\,000 each\, plus pitch coaching\, a finalist showcase\, and ongoin
 g access to fellowships and paid work through the Shifters 100 alumni netw
 ork. Free coaching is available from the moment you register\, so the payo
 ff to registering early is high. Submissions close 31 August 2026 (5pm UTC
 )\, with finalists announced in October and winners in December 2026. Appl
 y at https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Social Shifters\nLocation: Global\; open to youth-led ventures fro
 m anywhere in the world.\nAward: Multiple awards of up to USD 15\,000 each
  (reported grants from USD 3\,000 to USD 15\,000)\, plus pitch coaching\, 
 a finalist showcase\, free founder support from registration\, and ongoing
  access to fellowships and paid work through the Shifters 100 alumni netwo
 rk that corporate partners recruit from. Free to enter.\nDuration: Submiss
 ions close 31 August 2026\; finalists announced October\, winners December
  2026\n\nMore: https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Global\; open to youth-led ventures from anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ernest-solvay-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: King Baudouin Foundation: Ernest Solvay Fund 2026 (Call f
 or Projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Ernest Solvay Fund provides financial support for local-imp
 act initiatives in three areas: scientific education (science\, technology
 \, engineering and mathematics)\, planet progress (environmental initiativ
 es) and better life (community well-being). ELIGIBILITY: organisations sub
 mitting a project must implement it within a 100 km radius of a Solvay ind
 ustrial\, R&I or administrative site. FUNDING: up to EUR 10\,000 per initi
 ative\; the Fund covers expenses incurred only after the results are annou
 nced (mid-December 2026) and will not reimburse expenses incurred beforeha
 nd. APPLY: create or log in to an account at https://candidate.kbs-frb.be 
 and complete the online application form (it can be saved and completed in
  several stages). Applications are open 15 April 2026 to 30 September 2026
 \; results announced mid-December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Ernest Solv
 ay\, managed with the support of the King Baudouin Foundation\nLocation: O
 rganisations implementing a project within a 100 km radius of a Solvay ind
 ustrial\, R&I or administrative site\nAward: Up to EUR 10\,000 per initiat
 ive. Funding covers only expenses incurred after the results are announced
  (mid-December 2026)\; already-incurred expenses are not reimbursed. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Project implemented after mid-December 2026 anno
 uncement\n\nMore: https://kbs-frb.be/en/2026-ernest-solvay-fund?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kbs-frb.be/en/2026-ernest-solvay-fund?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Organisations implementing a project within a 100 km radius of a S
 olvay industrial\, R&I or administrative site
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-international-vouchers-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count). The inviting foreig
 n party must cover a proportionate share of the costs. Covers hourly fees\
 , travel and accommodation directly related to the activity. IMPORTANT TIM
 ING RULE: applications are accepted from 5 months to a minimum of 7 weeks 
 before the activity begins\, and processing takes about 6 weeks. This lead
  time can rule out activities that fall shortly after a round opens. Round
  2 (4 May to 22 June 2026) has closed. Round 3 runs 8 September 2026 15:00
  CEST to 27 October 2026 16:00 CEST\, with a budget of EUR 33\,000\; given
  the 7-week rule it effectively serves activities starting from late Octob
 er 2026 onwards. IMPORTANT PREREQUISITE: you must already have had an appl
 ication to the Fund positively assessed within the past five years\, and a
  previous voucher does not satisfy this\, so this is not a viable first ap
 proach to the Fund. The window runs 8 September 2026\, 15:00 CEST to 27 Oc
 tober 2026\, but closes early once 20 complete applications are received. 
 Maximum one voucher per applicant per calendar year.\n\nOrganisation: Stim
 uleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocation:
  Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within Eur
 ope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per trip
 \n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-voucher
 s?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:longview-digital-minds-grants-applied-work-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
SUMMARY:Deadline: Longview Philanthropy: Digital Minds Grants for Applied W
 ork 2026
DESCRIPTION:Longview Philanthropy invites proposals for applied work on the
  potential consciousness\, sentience\, moral status\, or experiences of AI
  systems. Typical grants are $50\,000–$2\,000\,000 per project\, with pr
 oposals outside that range considered when justified. New organisations ma
 y also receive some operational support. ELIGIBLE ACTIVITIES: seed funding
  for new organisations (think tanks\, research bodies\, initiatives)\; men
 torship programmes for researchers entering the digital minds field\; inte
 rnships\, new hires\, or focused programmes on digital minds at existing A
 I organisations\, academic labs\, or policy institutions\; convenings and 
 field-building (workshops\, conferences\, summits\, working groups address
 ing technical and governance questions). AREAS OF INTEREST: measuring AI w
 elfare\; consciousness and sentience research\; governance and legal/socia
 l science frameworks for potentially sentient AI\; communications work for
  thoughtful public discourse\; research beyond the US\; support organisati
 ons and operations professionals for independent technical researchers. SE
 LECTION CRITERIA: potential impact\, track record\, demonstrated interest 
 in digital minds and its relationship to AI risk\, cost-effectiveness\, le
 gal compliance. Deadline: 10 July 2026. Questions: digitalminds-rfp@longvi
 ew.org. Apply at https://www.longview.org/request-for-proposals-research-a
 nd-applied-work-on-digital-minds/.\n\nOrganisation: Longview Philanthropy\
 nLocation: Worldwide / remote (grant-eligible countries listed in applicat
 ion form)\nAward: Typical grants $50\,000–$2\,000\,000 per project\; pro
 posals outside this range considered when the work justifies it. May inclu
 de some operational support for new organisations. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Project-based\; duration varies by scope.\n\nMore: https://www.lon
 gview.org/request-for-proposals-research-and-applied-work-on-digital-minds
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.longview.org/request-for-proposals-research-and-applied-wor
 k-on-digital-minds/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
LOCATION:Worldwide / remote (grant-eligible countries listed in application
  form)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fujifilm-gfx-challenge-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151548Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: FUJIFILM GFX Challenge Grant Program 2026
DESCRIPTION:The GFX Challenge Grant Program\, sponsored by FUJIFILM and run
 ning since 2021\, awards 5 Global Grant Awards (USD 10\,000) and 10 Region
 al Grant Awards (USD 5\,000) to help aspiring creatives bring imaging proj
 ects to life. It is designed to nurture emerging and promising content cre
 ators\, giving them the opportunity to create content on topics with signi
 ficant meaning to them while gaining experience with FUJIFILM GFX System g
 ear\, including the GFX ETERNA 55 filmmaking camera. Proposed projects may
  be submitted as still photography or in movie format. AWARDS: both tiers 
 include complimentary use of a GFX System camera body and two GF lenses fo
 r the duration of the project\, plus mentoring and technical assistance fr
 om Fujifilm technicians and product experts. At the end of the production 
 period in May 2027\, recipients' final content is showcased on fujifilm-x.
 com\, with a series of exhibitions planned in various countries. ELIGIBILI
 TY: open to both amateur and professional photographers and videographers 
 who are residents of the countries/regions listed in the Entry Submission 
 section of the program page\; not open to employees or officers of FUJIFIL
 M and its subsidiaries. TO APPLY: combine three items into a single PDF: (
 1) the preformatted cover letter (downloadable from the program page)\; (2
 ) the project proposal covering descriptive plan\, objectives\, evaluation
  and outcome measures\, communications\, how you will use the Fujifilm par
 tnership and mentoring\, schedule\, and budget\; (3) a portfolio for each 
 individual involved. Proposals must be in English (optionally accompanied 
 by a version in your own language\; language proficiency is not judged). E
 ntry period 16 June to 17 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: FUJIFILM\nLocation
 : Open to residents of the countries/regions listed under Entry Submission
  on the program page. Final content showcased on fujifilm-x.com plus plann
 ed exhibitions in various countries.\nAward: 5 Global Grant Awards of USD 
 10\,000 and 10 Regional Grant Awards of USD 5\,000. All recipients also ge
 t complimentary use of a GFX System camera body (including the FUJIFILM GF
 X ETERNA 55 filmmaking camera) and two GF lenses for the duration of the p
 roject\, plus mentoring and technical assistance from Fujifilm technicians
  and product experts. Total approximate retail value of all awards: USD 22
 9\,500. No purchase necessary\; no entry fee.\nDuration: Application windo
 w 16 June to 17 August 2026. Production period concludes in May 2027\, aft
 er which final content is showcased on fujifilm-x.com and in a planned ser
 ies of exhibitions.\n\nMore: https://www.fujifilm-x.com/global/gfx-challen
 ge-grant-program/year-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://www.fujifilm-x.com/global/gfx-challenge-grant-program/year-2026
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open to residents of the countries/regions listed under Entry Subm
 ission on the program page. Final content showcased on fujifilm-x.com plus
  planned exhibitions in various countries.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
